\text{The coefficient of } x^3 \text{ is } ^7C_4 2^3 k^4 = 35 \times 8k^4 = 280k^4 \quad \dots (1)
\text{The coefficient of } x \text{ is } ^7C_6 2k^6 = 7 \times 2k^6 = 16k^6 \quad \dots (2)
(1) \text{ is } 10 \text{ times larger than } (2), \text{ so } 280k^4 = 10 \times 16k^6
\therefore 28k^4 = 16k^6
\therefore k^2 = \frac{7}{4} \quad \{k \neq 0\}
\therefore k = \frac{\sqrt{7}}{2} \quad \{k > 0\}

(3x^2-7)(x-2)^3 = (3x^2-7)(x^3 - 6x^2 + 12x - 8) \quad \{\text{using a}\}
\text{So, the terms containing } x^3 \text{ are } 36x^3 \text{ from } 3x^2(12x) \text{ and } -7x^3 \text{ from } -7(x^3)
\therefore \text{the coefficient of } x^3 \text{ is } 36 - 7 = 29.
